comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:58:08.644Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: four replication sets cover get selectors, bounded annotations, author coordinates, and health refresh. The gate exercises real temporary Git worktrees, malformed manifests, waiver combinations, refusal drift, branch detection, and default/custom main behavior. It is registered in quality:static and the release gate registry; all gates pass with zero applied waivers."
  "2026-08-07T14:59:34.768Z","harness:codex","Changelog evidence: latest registry pm-changelog 2026.8.7 installed and generated CHANGELOG.md from 1,959 closed items; the immediate --check rerun reported unchanged."
  "2026-08-07T15:11:49.371Z","harness:codex","PR #929 first hosted round at 5115f706b: Linux coverage shard 3/4 and Windows Node 24 both exposed the same shallow-checkout failure in the default changed-file test. CodeRabbit also identified missing changed-member enforcement, ISO waiver validation, absent src/cli handling, and zero-denominator declaration guards. Reopened for one cohesive gate correction."
  "2026-08-07T15:13:02.794Z","harness:codex","Review evidence linkage correction: docs/README.md and both changed release integration test files are now explicitly linked to this canonical item in addition to their runnable test command."
  "2026-08-07T15:24:30.844Z","harness:codex","Review implementation evidence: required_changed_members now fails a set when any declared recurrence member is absent from the activating changeset; waivers require real YYYY-MM-DD dates and remain queryable; zero/negative caps fail closed; missing src/cli is an empty census but all other read errors propagate; bare --changed-files is an explicit empty changeset so detached shallow CI does not depend on origin/main. Focused negative controls pass."
  "2026-08-07T15:48:45.220Z","harness:codex","Final verification: linked release/runtime and unit gates passed through pm test; repository coverage passed 49,851/49,851 statements, 36,296/36,296 branches, 10,209/10,209 functions, and 48,286/48,286 lines; static, contract, docs, package-artifact, secret, audit, and isolated entrypoint-cost gates passed."
  "2026-08-07T15:54:26.930Z","harness:codex","Post-close negative control: ISO-shaped but unparseable waiver dates (for example month 99) now short-circuit before Date normalization instead of throwing. The focused gate remains 100/100/100/100 and the final global run passes 49,851 statements, 36,297 branches, 10,209 functions, and 48,286 lines with zero uncovered counts."
  "2026-08-07T16:35:53.838Z","harness:codex","Final review correction: annotation-mutation-receipts now requires src/sdk/cli-contracts/tool-parameter-tables.ts in every activated changeset. A negative control changes src/sdk/annotations.ts alone and asserts the table-specific unchanged violation. The table now publishes comments/notes/learnings action-scoped full-history descriptions, the generated contract snapshot is current, quality:static reports all 12 members changed with zero waivers, and final coverage is exact 100/100/100/100."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:58:09.214Z","harness:codex","Cross-layer work is reliably complete only when the repository declares the expected replication set and activates enforcement from the changed diff. Prose checklists cannot detect a forgotten completion, MCP schema, export, or integration test."
  "2026-08-07T15:48:45.775Z","harness:codex","A replication gate must distinguish automatic Git discovery from an explicitly empty changeset, require the intended recurrence members to be present in the PR diff, and make any exception both expiring and queryable."
  "2026-08-07T16:35:54.357Z","harness:codex",A replication member that is merely declared and content-checked can still be skipped by a real feature diff; recurrence gates must also require that member in the activating changeset and prove the exact omission with a negative control.
